{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549490-magical-damage-again","id":1549490,"title":"Magical damage again","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-03-21T16:47:17-07:00","id":1549490,"title":"Magical damage again","content":"So 3 situations:<br /> <br /> 1. The mage creates a sword of light<br /> 2. The mage enchances his pistol shot with forces<br /> 3. the mage casts lightning<br /> <br /> lets say they all have 5 successes. How much damage will those effects deal?<br /> I assume 3 will follow standard damage table but what about 1 and 2? The book sugests for some reason that prime weapons deal only 1 damage per success but is that correct? How about enhancing actual weapons? Do we count their basic damage? How about the users STR? If not then why not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-23T12:13:22-07:00","id":1549524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549490-magical-damage-again#post1549490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So 3 situations:<br /> <br /> 1. The mage creates a sword of light<br /> 2. The mage enchances his pistol shot with forces<br /> 3. the mage casts lightning<br /> <br /> lets say they all have 5 successes. How much damage will those effects deal?<br /> I assume 3 will follow standard damage table but what about 1 and 2? The book sugests for some reason that prime weapons deal only 1 damage per success but is that correct? How about enhancing actual weapons? Do we count their basic damage? How about the users STR? If not then why not?</div> </div> </div> </div>1- Depends on how many successes the ST requires as base for creation of the sword. I'd say something like 3, so 5 successes makes a sword dealing Str+2 damage, if is tangible light and strength enters as a factor. <br /> Really depends on how the spell is made, the above explanation would be a Forces effect.<br /> <br /> Prime weapons deal damage as per the chart, so the sword would deal 10 aggravated damage and cost 1 quintessence per turn.<br /> <br /> 2- Each success can enhance 1 damage as per hdydt, so enhancement adds 5 damage levels to the regular pistol damage.<br /> <br /> 3- 5 successes means 10 damage. Lightning means a Forces attack, so 12 levels of aggravated damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-23T13:38:36-07:00","id":1549527,"title":"","content":"Electric damage isn't inherently agg in the books, so that could just be lethal. Also depending on how you go about &quot;casts lightning&quot; it may be an aimed spell with the attendant checks to actually hit the target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-23T14:32:39-07:00","id":1549528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549490-magical-damage-again?p=1549524#post1549524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1- Depends on how many successes the ST requires as base for creation of the sword. I'd say something like 3, so 5 successes makes a sword dealing Str+2 damage, if is tangible light and strength enters as a factor.<br /> Really depends on how the spell is made, the above explanation would be a Forces effect.<br /> <br /> Prime weapons deal damage as per the chart, so the sword would deal 10 aggravated damage and cost 1 quintessence per turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think i dont understand. Whats the difference between sword of light and a prime weapon?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 03-23-2025, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-23T14:34:17-07:00","id":1549529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549490-magical-damage-again?p=1549527#post1549527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Electric damage isn't inherently agg in the books, so that could just be lethal. Also depending on how you go about &quot;casts lightning&quot; it may be an aimed spell with the attendant checks to actually hit the target.</div> </div> </div> </div>This depends on edition. M20 has electricity, fire and Prime as aggravated. Can't remember other editions right now...<br /> <br /> And yes thrown/shot spells require hitting and might allow for dodge, so this depends entirely on how you build your effect and your paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-23T14:37:38-07:00","id":1549530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549490-magical-damage-again?p=1549528#post1549528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think i dont understand. Whats the difference between sword of light and a prime weapon?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can create a weapon made of solid light with Forces, for example. There are no hard rules for those, I would rule like in my answer.<br /> <br /> Prime weapons are not tangible and have their own rules, which is the one I posted (Arete x2 dmg and 1 quint per turn)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-23T14:57:42-07:00","id":1549531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549490-magical-damage-again?p=1549530#post1549530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can create a weapon made of solid light with Forces, for example. There are no hard rules for those, I would rule like in my answer.<br /> <br /> Prime weapons are not tangible and have their own rules, which is the one I posted (Arete x2 dmg and 1 quint per turn)</div> </div> </div> </div>Does the prime weapon sword add str ? if not then why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-23T15:40:06-07:00","id":1549533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549490-magical-damage-again?p=1549531#post1549531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does the prime weapon sword add str ? if not then why?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not very clear to me, but I would saybit doesn't. In M20 description of the rank 3 of Prime, the weapons are described as dealing the regular damage chart. So Arete successes x2 and that's it. I see it as an intangible burning primordial flame, burning through anything in its path.<br /> <br /> Forces is the sphere that mess with\u2026well, forces. So you can give tangibility to something, just like you can control forces to give illusions the sense of touch.<br /> <br /> Can you make a tangible sword with Prime that adds strength to damage? Well, maybe. But personally, I'd rule the damage similar to my Forces sword and not str+Arete successes x2, that'd be too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}